sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant F as :Frontend
  participant G as :Gems
  participant P as :Google Places API
  participant DB as :Database

  U->>F: open the discovery map
  F->>+G: GET /gem/within (visible map area)
  opt map area valid
    G->>+DB: find the gems in the area, highest Gem Score first
    DB-->>-G: gems, or an error
  end
  G-->>-F: 200 [gems], 400 "Invalid bounds.", or 500 "Get Gems failed."
  alt 200 gems
    F-->>U: a marker per gem
  else 400 area too large (e.g. crosses the date line)
    F-->>U: "Zoom in to see gems"
  else 500 database error
    F-->>U: "Couldn't load gems, try again"
  end

  U->>F: tap the marker of gem places/{pk}
  F->>+G: GET /gem?name=places/{pk}
  G->>+DB: find the gem
  DB-->>-G: gem, none, or an error
  G-->>-F: 200 gem, 404 "No such Gem.", or 500 "Get Gem failed."
  alt 200 gem
    F-->>U: half-height panel with name, type and Gem Score
    U->>F: pull the panel up to full screen
    F->>+G: GET /gem/{pk}/photo
    G->>+DB: find the gem's photo
    DB-->>-G: photo name, or none
    opt the gem has a photo
      G->>+P: image URL for the photo
      P-->>-G: short-lived image URL, or error
    end
    G-->>-F: 302 redirect to the image, 404 "No photo.", 502 "Google Places unavailable.", or 500 "Get photo failed."
    alt 302 image
      F-->>U: photo, type, description, Gem Score and number of ratings
    else 404, 502 or 500
      F-->>U: placeholder image, with the other details
    end
  else 404 gem deleted since the map loaded
    F-->>U: "This gem is no longer available", marker removed
  else 500 database error
    F-->>U: "Couldn't load this gem, try again"
  end
  Note over U,DB: If the server can't be reached, the Frontend shows "No connection, try again"
